API Summary (for frontend integration)

POST /api/analyze
Purpose: Run immediate analysis on a provided text and return results synchronously.
Method: POST
Headers:
Content-Type: application/json
Request body:
JSON: { "text": "<journal entry text>" }
text must be a non-empty string.
Success response:
Status: 200 OK
JSON body (object) with keys:
distortions: array of rule-based distortion objects (type, severity, confidence, excerpt, explanation, reframe)
overallScore: integer 0-100 (higher is healthier; mapped from model distortion score when model available)
positivePatterns: array of strings
model: (optional) object with ML analyzer output (present when model loaded). Contains:
text: original text
is_distorted: bool
distortion_score: float (0.0–1.0)
distortions_detected: dict (model-detected types → counts/examples)
emotion_analysis: object:
emotions: dict label→score (probabilities)
primary_emotion: string
primary_emotion_score: float
vader_sentiment: {pos, neu, neg, compound}
textblob_sentiment: {polarity, subjectivity}
overall_sentiment: "positive"|"neutral"|"negative"
health_assessment: { concern_level, concerns (array), recommendation }
Error responses:
400 Bad Request if body missing or not JSON or missing 'text' string.
500 Internal Server Error if unexpected error (rare; model errors are caught and a fallback result is returned).
Example request (PowerShell):
$body = @{ text = "I made a mistake and now I'm sure I'm a failure." } | ConvertTo-Json
Invoke-RestMethod -Uri 'http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/analyze' -Method Post -ContentType 'application/json' -Body $body
Example minimal success response (abridged):
{
"distortions":[{"type":"All-or-Nothing Thinking","severity":"high","confidence":90,"excerpt":"I always","explanation":"...","reframe":"..."}],
"overallScore":12,
"positivePatterns":[],
"model":{
"text":"I made a mistake...",
"is_distorted":true,
"distortion_score":0.88,
"distortions_detected":{...},
"emotion_analysis":{"emotions":{"anger":0.6,"sadness":0.3},"primary_emotion":"anger","vader_sentiment":{...},"overall_sentiment":"negative"},
"health_assessment":{"concern_level":"high","concerns":["..."],"recommendation":"..."}
}
}
POST /api/entries
Purpose: Create a new journal entry (persists entry immediately) and optionally kick off background analysis.
Method: POST
Headers:
Content-Type: application/json
Request body:
JSON: { "text": "<journal text>", "mood": "<optional>", "meta": { ... } }
Only text is required and must be a string.
Success response:
Status: 201 Created
JSON body:
id: string (entry id)
text: string (stored text)
createdAt: ISO timestamp (UTC)
summary: optional string (short first-sentence summary)
Behavior:
Immediately stores entry via storage.create_entry_record.
Starts a background Thread to compute analysis and call storage.set_entry_analysis(entry_id, analysis) — analysis runs asynchronously; this endpoint returns before analysis finishes.
Error responses:
400 Bad Request if invalid JSON or missing/invalid text.
Example request (PowerShell):
$body = @{ text = "Today felt awful..." } | ConvertTo-Json
Invoke-RestMethod -Uri 'http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/entries' -Method Post -ContentType 'application/json' -Body $body
Example success response:
{ "id":"abc123", "text":"Today felt awful...", "createdAt":"2025-11-10T12:34:56Z", "summary":"Today felt awful." }
GET /api/entries
Purpose: List stored entries (lightweight list view).
Method: GET
Query: none
Success response:
Status: 200 OK
JSON body: array of item objects, sorted by createdAt descending. Each item contains:
id: string
text: string (full text — trimmed if needed)
createdAt: ISO timestamp
optional: score (if present in storage)
optional: summary (if present)
Example response:
[ { "id":"abc123","text":"...","createdAt":"2025-11-10T12:34:56Z","summary":"..." }, ... ]
GET /api/analysis/<entry_id>
Purpose: Retrieve analysis for a previously created entry (if analysis not yet ready, trigger background analysis and return pending).
Method: GET
Path params:
entry_id: string id from POST /api/entries
Success responses:
200 OK with JSON body: the analysis object that was stored earlier by the background job (same shape as returned by compute_analysis_for_text): it will include distortions, overallScore, positivePatterns, and model when model available.
202 Accepted with JSON body { "status": "pending" } if no analysis is present yet; a background thread is kicked to start analysis.
Error response:
404 Not Found if entry id does not exist.
Example:
GET /api/analysis/abc123 → either full analysis (200) or { "status":"pending" } (202)
General notes and tips for frontend Copilot

Content-Type must be application/json for POST endpoints.
The model field may not be present if the ML analyzer failed or model not loaded; code defensively.
First-ever call that requires the ML model may be slow (model download and load). Consider:
Calling a warm-up endpoint (or get_analyzer() at backend startup) to download and cache the model before users hit the service.
For lightweight UI needs, prefer reading model['emotion_analysis']['primary_emotion'] and model['emotion_analysis']['overall_sentiment'] when present.
The rule-based distortions include human-friendly explanation and reframe text useful for display.
If you need a smaller payload for the UI, use /api/analyze and have the frontend read specific keys and discard the rest.
